<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Lower Bound). ‣ 4 Coverage Guarantees ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given the data <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, define a random index <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{1,\ldots,n+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{1,\ldots,n+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> from the multinomial distribution</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\mid\{(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})\}\sim\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{i}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∼</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\mid\{(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})\}\sim\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{i}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of the prediction set <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C}_{n}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C}_{n}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\iff S_{n+1}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{S_{i}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\iff S_{n+1}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{S_{i}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the assumption that <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq\max_{i=1,\ldots,n}\widehat{w}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq\max_{i=1,\ldots,n}\widehat{w}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely, we can verify that for almost all <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{S_{i}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{S_{i}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\infty}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow S_{n+1}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow S_{n+1}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow\mathbf{S}^{K}_{K}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow\mathbf{S}^{K}_{K}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\delta_{\mathbf{S}^{K}_{i}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define a set-valued function <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}:\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\to 2^{\{1,\ldots,n+1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}:\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\to 2^{\{1,\ldots,n+1\}}</annotation></semantics></math> by for any <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(s)=\left\{i\in\{1,\ldots,n+1\}:s_{i}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{j}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{k}+\lambda}\delta_{s_{j}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{k}+\lambda}\delta_{s_{n+1}}\right)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(s)=\left\{i\in\{1,\ldots,n+1\}:s_{i}&gt;{\rm Quantile}\left(1-\alpha;\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{\widehat{w}_{j}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{k}+\lambda}\delta_{s_{j}}+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{k}+\lambda}\delta_{s_{n+1}}\right)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, a direct argument shows that for all <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{F}(s)}\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\leq\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{F}(s)}\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, by the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1})\Longrightarrow K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now compute</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathrm{P}}(K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K}))=\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{P}}\left(K=i\text{ and }i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathrm{P}}(K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K}))=\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{P}}\left(K=i\text{ and }i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[{\mathrm{P}}\left(K=i\mid(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[{\mathrm{P}}\left(K=i\mid(X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{n},Y_{n}),(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\left[\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S})\right)\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left(\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i\neq n+1)+\frac{\lambda}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\mathds{1}(i=n+1)\right)\left[\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}\left(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S})\right)\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\left[\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}))\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\left[\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}))\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\|\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\right\|_{\infty}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left\lvert\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}))\right\rvert\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\|\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\right\|_{\infty}{\mathrm{E}}\left[\left\lvert\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{i}))-\mathds{1}(i\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}))\right\rvert\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\|\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\right\|_{\infty}{\rm TV}(\mathbf{S}^{i},\mathbf{S})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\|\frac{\widehat{w}_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widehat{w}_{j}+\lambda}\right\|_{\infty}{\rm TV}(\mathbf{S}^{i},\mathbf{S}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">by <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{n+1}=\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{n+1}=\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and the definition of total variation distance.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of the first statement is complete by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{P}}(Y_{n+1}\in\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1}))=1-{\mathrm{P}}(Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1}))\geq 1-{\mathrm{P}}(K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{P}}(Y_{n+1}\in\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1}))=1-{\mathrm{P}}(Y_{n+1}\notin\widehat{C}_{n}(X_{n+1}))\geq 1-{\mathrm{P}}(K\in\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{S}^{K})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of the second statement is direct from the first statement since if in addition the scores <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1},\ldots,S_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1},\ldots,S_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm TV}(\mathbf{S}^{i},\mathbf{S})={\rm TV}((S_{1},\ldots,S_{n+1}),(S_{1},\ldots,S_{i-1},S_{n+1},S_{i+1},\ldots,S_{n},S_{i}))\leq 2{\rm TV}(S_{i},S_{n+1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm TV}(\mathbf{S}^{i},\mathbf{S})={\rm TV}((S_{1},\ldots,S_{n+1}),(S_{1},\ldots,S_{i-1},S_{n+1},S_{i+1},\ldots,S_{n},S_{i}))\leq 2{\rm TV}(S_{i},S_{n+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Upper Bound). ‣ 4 Coverage Guarantees ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Upper Bound). ‣ 4 Coverage Guarantees ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is similar to the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Lower Bound). ‣ 4 Coverage Guarantees ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which generalizes Theorem 3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Barber et al., (2023)</a></cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional experiments using the APS score, following the same experiment settings as the main text.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the number of instances in each of the 17 subjects in the MMLU benchmark. Figure <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> compares the empirical coverage of standard CP and DS-CP across all evaluated models. Figure <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports the average prediction set size for standard CP and DS-CP across all evaluated models. Figure <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Domain-Shift-Aware Conformal Prediction for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents the scatter plot of the empirical coverage of DS-CP versus standard CP across all subject pairs and models. Overall, APS-based results echo our LAC findings: DS-CP adaptively corrects under-coverage induced by domain shift while maintaining practical set sizes.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05566v1/mmlu_subject_distribution.svg" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/236;" width="471" height="236"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Distribution of MMLU instances across 17 subjects.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05566v1/aps_coverage_delta_violin.svg" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:471/471;" width="471" height="471"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Empirical coverage of CP vs. DS-CP across models. The center bar is the median.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05566v1/aps_setsize_hist.svg" id="A2.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:471/455;" width="471" height="455"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Average prediction set size of CP vs. DS-CP across models.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05566v1/aps_paired_coverage_scatter.svg" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:471/424;" width="471" height="424"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Paired coverage comparison of CP and DS-CP across models.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional details on the implementation of the experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset availability.</span> All MMLU data and logits for all evaluated models are reused from <a href="https://github.com/smartyfh/LLM-Uncertainty-Bench/tree/main" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/smartyfh/LLM-Uncertainty-Bench/tree/main</a>. We do not modify the underlying model predictions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training details.</span> For each model <span id="A3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model</span>, we load logits from <span id="A3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">outputs_base/
<br class="ltx_break">{model}_mmlu_10k_base_icl1.pkl</span> using a single prompt method (<span id="A3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">base</span>) and one in-context configuration (<span id="A3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">icl1</span>). We exclude a small set of item indices <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,3,5,7,9]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,3,5,7,9]</annotation></semantics></math> for consistency with our preprocessing. For DS-CP, we use the embedding model <span id="A3.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all-MiniLM-L6-v2</span> and density ratio estimation is obtained from the XGBoost classifier trained with
<span id="A3.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_depth</span>=3, <span id="A3.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_estimators</span>=50, <span id="A3.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">learning_rate</span>=0.2,
<span id="A3.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">subsample</span>=0.7, <span id="A3.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">colsample_bytree</span>=0.7, <span id="A3.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reg_alpha</span>=5,
<span id="A3.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reg_lambda</span>=10, <span id="A3.p3.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">random_state</span>=42, <span id="A3.p3.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_jobs</span>=1. No tuning is performed. All experiments were run locally on a MacBook Pro (14-inch, 2021) with an Apple M1 Pro chip, 16 GB RAM, and macOS Sequoia 15.5. No discrete GPU was used.</p>
</div>
